==============================================================================
Derived work
==============================================================================

Parts of this project are derived from the following MIT-licensed works. Their
copyright notices are retained here as that licence requires; the permission
notice and warranty disclaimer above apply to them on identical terms.

process-stutterjump -- Copyright (c) 2025 sevendc
  https://github.com/sevendc/process-stutterjump
  demo.html's WebGL bootstrap (the `with(g)` two-character aliasing of GL
  methods, the fullscreen-triangle setup), the `//*--` shader fence and the
  `// -- dev start/end` marker convention. build.js is a rewrite but follows
  the same extract/minify/pack pipeline.

Loertsy -- Copyright (c) 2019-2023 Timo Pitkänen
           Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Timo Pitkänen, Perttu Lamminmäki
  https://gitlab.com/bits_lab/loertsy
  The compeko backend in build.js: the `<svg onload>` bootstrap that re-fetches
  the page, slices off the header and inflates the appended deflate stream,
  ported from tools/combine_and_pack.py. Also the source of the patched Shader
  Minifier build in tools/shader-minifier/.

compeko.js -- Copyright (c) 2022-2024 0b5vr
  https://gist.github.com/0b5vr/09ee96ca2efbe5bf9d64dad7220e923b
  The original DecompressionStream self-extraction technique that Loertsy's
  packer, and therefore critter's compeko backend, is based on.


Redistributed binaries in tools/shader-minifier/ are covered separately by
tools/shader-minifier/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES (Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause).
Build-time npm dependencies are not redistributed and carry their own licences.
